    <string name="priv_que_datos">What data does StudyMate keep?</string>
    <string name="priv_que_datos_sub">What is stored and where</string>
    <string name="priv_que_datos_texto">• Your email and password are handled by Firebase Authentication (we never see your password).\n\n• Your profile (name, major, university, semester and photo), subjects, tasks and grades are stored in Firebase Realtime Database, in a space only your account can read.\n\n• The phone only keeps your preferences (reminders, time format, language and theme) and a copy of your reminders to reschedule them after a restart.\n\n• StudyMate never sells or shares your data.</string>
    <string name="priv_politica">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="priv_politica_sub">How we use your information</string>
    <string name="priv_politica_texto">StudyMate is a study planner built as a university project.\n\n1. What we collect: only what you type into the app (profile, subjects, schedules, tasks and grades) and your email to sign in.\n\n2. Why: to show your information on any phone where you sign in and to send you due date reminders.\n\n3. Who we share it with: nobody. Data is stored on Google Firebase services.\n\n4. Your rights: you can edit your profile, erase your academic data or delete your account at any time from the menu in Profile.\n\n5. Contact: write to us from Help &amp; support.</string>
