    <string name="ayuda_acerca_texto">StudyMate %1$s\n\nYour university planner: keep subjects, schedules, tasks and grades in one place, with reminders so you never miss a due date.\n\nMade with as a university project.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_asunto_soporte">StudyMate · Support</string>
    <string name="ayuda_asunto_problema">StudyMate · Problem report</string>
    <string name="ayuda_cuerpo_problema">Describe what happened and what you were doing:\n\n\n\n— Phone details (please keep) —\nApp version: %1$s\nAndroid: %2$s\nPhone: %3$s</string>
    <string name="ayuda_sin_correo">No email app found. Write to us at %1$s</string>

    <string-array name="faq_preguntas">
        <item>Why am I not getting reminders?</item>
        <item>How do I add a subject with its schedule?</item>
        <item>How is my average calculated?</item>
        <item>Will I lose my data if I change phones?</item>
        <item>How do I change my profile photo?</item>
        <item>I forgot my password, what do I do?</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="faq_respuestas">
        <item>Go to Profile → Menu → Notifications and make sure reminders are on and that the phone allows notifications. Some phones with battery saver delay alerts by a few minutes.</item>
        <item>Open the Subjects tab and tap \"+\". Enter the name and teacher, then add the class days and times.</item>
        <item>Inside each subject you record your grades with their weight. StudyMate calculates the subject\'s weighted average on a 0–5 scale (3.0 to pass).</item>
        <item>No. Everything is saved to your account in the cloud: sign in with the same email on the other phone and your information will be there.</item>
        <item>In the Profile tab tap your photo (or the emoji) and pick an image from your gallery. Tap it again to change or remove it.</item>
        <item>On the sign-in screen tap \"Forgot your password?\" and we\'ll email you. If you\'re already signed in, use Profile → Menu → Change password.</item>
    </string-array>

